title":"Investment Strategy Statement","url":"https://democracy.bexley.gov.uk/documents/s121976/investment-strategy-statement.pdf","committee":"Pensions Committee","date":"10/03/2026","key":false},{"title":"Appendix J - Feb 2026 - Treasury Management Strategy - Public Cabinet","url":"https://democracy.bexley.gov.uk/documents/s121734/appendix-j-feb-2026-treasury-management-strategy-public-cabi.pdf","committee":"Public Cabinet","date":"23/02/2026","key":true},{"title":"3 Appendix B - Capital Programme Monitoring - Public Cabinet P9","url":"https://democracy.bexley.gov.uk/documents/s121711/3-appendix-b-capital-programme-monitoring-public-cabinet-p9.pdf","committee":"Public Cabinet","date":"23/02/2026","key":true},{"title":"Appendix F - Feb 2026 - Capital Programme - Public Cabinet","url":"https://democracy.bexley.gov.uk/documents/s121730/appendix-f-feb-2026-capital-programme-public-cabinet.pdf","committee":"Public Cabinet","date":"23/02/2026","key":true}],"read_documents":[{"title":"Annual Treasury Management Outturn Report 2025/26","url":"https://bexley.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s125892/Item 8 LBB Treasury Outturn Report 2025-26 Final for GPAC.pdf","committee":"General Purposes and Audit Committee","date":"2026-07-29","category":"treasury","fy":"2025/26"}],"calendar":{"upcoming":[{"date":"2026-09-24","committee":"Pensions Committee","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.bexley.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-30","committee":"General Purposes and Audit Committee","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.bexley.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-06","committee":"Places Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.bexley.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-07","committee":"Adult Social Care & Health Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.bexley.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-13","committee":"Children's Services and Education Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.bexley.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-14","committee":"Finance & Corporate Services Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.bexley.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-21","committee":"Public Cabinet","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.bexley.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-04","committee":"Council","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.bexley.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-02","committee":"Bexley Standing Advisory Council on Religious Education (SACRE)","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.bexley.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-08","committee":"Finance & Corporate Services Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.bexley.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-15","committee":"Council","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.bexley.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-29","committee":"General Purposes and Audit Committee","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.bexley.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-31","committee":"Pensions Board","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.bexley.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Staff capacity constraints and outdated procedures identified as systemic issues","lead":"Staffing shortages and system limitations increase operational risk, error potential, and resilience concerns. They suggest the council may be under-resourced to maintain effective financial and operational controls, which affects credit quality.","iso":"2026-07-29","paper_title":"Item 10 Audit Report and Opinion GPAC 16.7.26","paper_url":"https://bexley.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s125886/125886.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Only 47% of prior audit recommendations fully implemented within a year","lead":"Low implementation of audit recommendations indicates either that management lacks capacity to address known control weaknesses or does not prioritize them. Either situation suggests systemic governance concerns that could affect financial controls and\u2026","iso":"2026-07-29","paper_title":"Item 10 Audit Report and Opinion GPAC 16.7.26","paper_url":"https://bexley.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s125886/125886.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Limited assurance opinions increased from 27% to 42% of audits year-on-year","lead":"Deteriorating audit opinion trends suggest the council's control environment is weakening rather than improving. This negative trajectory is a red flag for lenders assessing the council's governance maturity.","iso":"2026-07-29","paper_title":"Item 10 Audit Report and Opinion GPAC 16.7.26","paper_url":"https://bexley.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s125886/125886.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-07-29","committee":"General Purposes and Audit Committee","paper_title":"Item 10 Audit Report and Opinion GPAC 16.7.26","paper_url":"https://bexley.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s125886/125886.pdf","headline":"Staff capacity constraints and outdated procedures identified as systemic issues","detail":"Internal audit identified persistent cross-council themes including staff capacity challenges causing audit delays or inability to complete full scopes, lack of up-to-date policies and procedures, system limitations requiring manual workarounds, and persistent control failures (e.g., school payroll miscoding, unmanaged asset registers). One audit was carried over to 2026/27 due to staff absence on ill health grounds.","category":"people","matters":"Staffing shortages and system limitations increase operational risk, error potential, and resilience concerns. They suggest the council may be under-resourced to maintain effective financial and operational controls, which affects credit quality.","figures":"Common themes included staff absence causing audit delays; no quantified staffing levels provided","quote":"Staff capacity challenges which cause delays in work undertaken or the inability to undertake full scopes of work","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-29","committee":"General Purposes and Audit Committee","paper_title":"Item 10 Audit Report and Opinion GPAC 16.7.26","paper_url":"https://bexley.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s125886/125886.pdf","headline":"Only 47% of prior audit recommendations fully implemented within a year","detail":"Follow-up testing of 32 prior-year recommendations found only 47% (15 audits) fully implemented, 44% partially implemented, and 9% with no evidence of action. Even Priority 1 (urgent) recommendations showed weak implementation, with only 2 of 3 fully completed.","category":"governance","matters":"Low implementation of audit recommendations indicates either that management lacks capacity to address known control weaknesses or does not prioritize them. Either situation suggests systemic governance concerns that could affect financial controls and service delivery.","figures":"47% (15) fully implemented, 44% (14) partially implemented, with 2 Priority 1 recommendations and 1 of 3 Priority 1 recommendations fully implemented","quote":"Of the recommendations tested, 47% (15) were fully implemented (of which 2 were Priority 1) and 44% were partially implemented (of which 1 was a Priority 1).","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-29","committee":"General Purposes and Audit Committee","paper_title":"Item 10 Audit Report and Opinion GPAC 16.7.26","paper_url":"https://bexley.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s125886/125886.pdf","headline":"Limited assurance opinions increased from 27% to 42% of audits year-on-year","detail":"In 2025/26, 42% of general assurance reviews received 'limited assurance' ratings (meaning significant weaknesses requiring improvement), compared to 27% in 2024/25. Simultaneously, 'substantial assurance' opinions fell from 9% to 4%, showing fewer areas of strong control across the council.","category":"audit","matters":"Deteriorating audit opinion trends suggest the council's control environment is weakening rather than improving. This negative trajectory is a red flag for lenders assessing the council's governance maturity.","figures":"2025/26: 4% Substantial, 54% Reasonable, 42% Limited; 2024/25: 9% Substantial, 64% Reasonable, 27% Limited","quote":"As a percentage % / Year Substantial Reasonable Limited No / 2025/26 4% 54% 42% 0% / 2024/25 9% 64% 27% 0%","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-29","committee":"General Purposes and Audit Committee","paper_title":"Item 10 Audit Report and Opinion GPAC 16.7.26","paper_url":"https://bexley.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s125886/125886.pdf","headline":"Audit opinion was borderline between reasonable and limited assurance","detail":"The council received a 'reasonable' overall audit opinion on its governance, risk management, and control arrangements for 2025/26. However, the report explicitly states the opinion was 'borderline with the limited opinion,' meaning a small number of additional weaknesses would have triggered a downgrade to limited assurance, which signals significant control gaps.","category":"audit","matters":"A borderline opinion indicates the council's control environment is adequate but fragile. For lenders, this suggests governance structures are on the edge of acceptability; any material deterioration could result in a limited opinion, which would be a material warning sign.","figures":"The opinion was borderline with limited assurance","quote":"The opinion was borderline with the limited opinion.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-29","committee":"General Purposes and Audit Committee","paper_title":"Item 9 GP + Audit Committee 29 July 2026 LGA Finance peer challenge Final report","paper_url":"https://bexley.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s125891/125891.pdf","headline":"New section 151 officer appointed but not yet in post at time of review; arrival expected to strengthen financial grip","detail":"The peer team noted that the arrival of the new section 151 officer (appointed but not in post at the time of the FPC) will provide stability and strengthen the financial services team and bring a renewed focus on structure and governance. This leadership transition is material for financial management continuity.","category":"governance","matters":"A lender should track whether the new CFO brings the financial discipline and strategic capability needed to execute the council's multi-year financial plan; leadership changes at this level are material to credit risk","figures":"new section 151 officer appointed at the time of review but not yet in post","quote":"the arrival of the new section 151 officer (appointed but not in post at the time of the FPC) will provide stability and strengthen the financial services team and will bring a renewed focus on structure and governance","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-07-29"},"name":"Bexley","findings_total":75,"news_drafts_total":3}}